  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1238 PM CST Mon Nov 16 2026\n\nRidging slides eastward into the Ohio Valley on Wednesday as a\nRex or High over Low Block across the Mid Atlantic and \nsoutheastern US through Wednesday night. It will be windy and \nwarm on Wednesday. Winds will be southerly at 10 to 20 MPH with \ngusts up to 30 MPH. A fast moving short wave is forecast to \nlive northeastward across the area Wednesday night into \nThursday morning. Moisture is limited and the best lift is to \nthe northwest of the area. Precipitation is expected to limited \nto a few sprinkles with model QPF showing little if any \nprecipitation. \n\nDeep southwesterly flow aloft is forecast to continue into the\nupcoming weekend as a dampening 500 MPH shortwave lifts across\nthe area. Models vary in the tilt of the shortwave and its\nintensity. Currently, the NBM has a 10 to 30 percent chance of\nat least a tenth of an inch with the best chances in far \nnorthwest Illinois on Saturday. This wave is forecast to bring a\ncold front across the area during the day. HIgh temperatures on\nSaturday will be in the lower to mid 60s Saturday will be \nanother windy day with southerly winds of 10 to 20 MPH and gusts\nof 25 to 30 MPH. It will turn noticeably cooler behind the \nfront on Sunday with high temperatures about 20 degrees colder.",
